KNN Regression

To predict at \(x_0\), average the responses of the \(K\) closest training points: \(\hat f(x_0) = \dfrac1K\sum_{x_i\in\mathcal N_0} y_i\).
Small \(K\): very flexible (low bias, high variance). Large \(K\): smooth (high bias, low variance).


knn_reg &lt;- function(xtrain, ytrain, xtest, k) {
  xtrain &lt;- as.matrix(xtrain); xtest &lt;- as.matrix(xtest)
  apply(xtest, 1, function(x0) {
    d &lt;- sqrt(colSums((t(xtrain) - x0)^2))
    mean(ytrain[order(d)[1:k]])
  })
}

Golden-Section Search by Hand
Keep a bracket \([a,b]\) and two interior points at the golden ratio \(\phi = (\sqrt5 - 1)/2\); each step discards a fraction \(1-\phi\approx 0.382\) of the bracket using one new function evaluation.

golden &lt;- function(f, a, b, tol = 1e-8) {
  phi &lt;- (sqrt(5) - 1) / 2; x1 &lt;- b - phi * (b - a); x2 &lt;- a + phi * (b - a); f1 &lt;- f(x1); f2 &lt;- f(x2); k &lt;- 0
  while (b - a &gt; tol) {
    k &lt;- k + 1
    if (f1 &gt; f2) { b &lt;- x2; x2 &lt;- x1; f2 &lt;- f1; x1 &lt;- b - phi * (b - a); f1 &lt;- f(x1) }   # maximize
    else         { a &lt;- x1; x1 &lt;- x2; f1 &lt;- f2; x2 &lt;- a + phi * (b - a); f2 &lt;- f(x2) }
  }
  c(maximum = (a + b) / 2, iterations = k)
}
